You can use the "as const" syntax to tell the type system that you know a value will always have a specific type.

For example, you can use "as const" to tell the type system that a value will always be a string, even though it might technically be any type:

```
let myString: string = "Hello";
let myNumber: number = 42;
let myUnion: string | number = "Hello";

