Here is a Java solution without loops or recursion:
```java
public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) return false;
    int power = 1;
    while (power <= n) power *= 3;
    return power / 3 == n;
}
```

This works by calculating powers of 3 and checking if we reach the input number. 
For example, for n = 27:

power = 1  ->  1 < 27, continue
power = 3  ->  3 < 27, continue 
power = 9  ->  9 < 27, continue
power = 27 -> 27 = 27, return true

For n = 0 or a negative number, we will never reach it with the powers of 3, so we return false.

Time complexity: O(log n) since we are doubling the power each time. 
Space complexity: O(1)

